finding: Live sibling views are not refreshed after another World grows the shared kernel memory. src/standard/physics/world/body.ts:206-215 returns resident sim/state objects without refreshing their BodyStore; src/standard/physics/kernel/bodycolumns.ts:374-391 reads its held stateF directly. Reproduction: one owner World, PhysicsWorld A with one dynamic sphere at (1,2,3), velocity (7,0,0), step once; create PhysicsWorld B on that owner and 2000 dynamic spheres. Kernel memory grows from 1376256 to 4980736 bytes. A.getPosition() and A.getLinearVelocity() change from numeric values to {x:undefined,y:undefined,z:undefined}, remaining invalid after B.destroy(). A ray query in isolation.node.ts refreshes the stores before every tick, concealing this case. Stage 1 must leave a live sibling usable across allocation and destroy/recreate, without requiring an unrelated query to rebind its views.
